course: dictionary
lesson: 2977
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Dub is one of them, so the words around it tell you which meaning is right. Always check the context first.
explain: «They dubbed him the Wizard.» Here dub means to give someone a name or a nickname. Try swapping in named: «They named him the Wizard» still makes sense.
explain: «The Japanese cartoons were dubbed into English.» Here dub means to replace the voices with voices in another language. The clues are cartoons and English, so the voices have changed.
explain: Through a doctor's stethoscope the heartbeat sounds like lub-dub. This dub is only a sound, not a name or a change of voices. Context tells you which meaning you need.
fact: Dub is a verb and a noun. As a noun, dub is a kind of music.
fact: To dub a film or TV show means to replace its voices with voices in another language, or to add sounds to it.
fact: To dub someone means to give them a nickname or a name, as in «They dubbed him the Wizard».
fact: To dub a knight means to make someone a knight by touching his shoulders with a sword.
fact: Dub is a kind of reggae music from Jamaica, with lots of echo and bass.
exercise: «They dubbed him the Wizard.» What does dubbed mean here? | *Gave him a name | Put him in a box | Took his photo | Hit him with a wand
exercise: «The Japanese cartoons were dubbed into English.» What has changed? | The ending | The size of the screen | *The voices | The colours
exercise: Dub is a kind of music from Jamaica. What is it known for? | *Lots of echo and bass | Songs sung in church | Silence with no sound at all | Loud trumpets and drums only
test: «The king dubbed the brave man a knight.» What did the king do? | Asked the man to sing | Gave him a horse and a castle | Sent him away from the court | *Touched his shoulders with a sword to make him a knight
test: «The children dubbed the tall tree the Giant.» What does dubbed mean? | Painted it green | *Gave it a nickname | Measured its height | Chopped it down
exam: In «The film was dubbed into Spanish», which of these has changed? | Its length | *Its voices | Its director | Its title
